# Compass UI guidance

Jules selected Linear as the visual foundation across Compass and authorised implementation on 10 September 2026. Use a near-white working area, quiet grey navigation, consistent sans-serif typography, restrained violet-blue actions, broad operational views and comfortable writing measures. The previous cream/orange editorial direction is superseded for the operator console.

Current design contract: `docs/design/WORKSPACE.md`. Shared owners: `src/app/folio.css` compatibility tokens/styles, `src/app/workspace.css` shared sizing and hierarchy, `src/components/OperatorShell.tsx` and `src/components/folio/FolioChrome.tsx`. Page-specific workspace styles extend these owners. Keep existing data, auth, caching and persistence contracts unless the request includes their behaviour.

A request to improve UI or UX authorises relevant changes to hierarchy, spacing, layout, feedback and interaction within the requested surface. Make the result meaningfully better and explain the evidence. It does not require preserving a demonstrated usability problem. Separate verified defects from design proposals; a framework is not the verdict.

Use actual current source values and rendered evidence. Keep keyboard operation, visible errors, narrow-screen scrolling and draft safety intact. A completed build or a mockup alone is not evidence that the deployed interface works.
